        "import_module": "sciona.atoms.numerical.statistics.central_mean",
        "source_symbol": "central_rank_mean",
        "description": "Sort each column and average a caller-sized central rank interval. Rows are observations and columns independent quantities. Require at least one row, finite real numeric values and a Python integer retained count in [1, rows]. Zero columns return an empty float64 vector. Convert to a fresh column-contiguous float64 matrix, sort ascending, then apply NumPy mean to ranks [floor((rows-retained)/2), floor((rows-retained)/2)+retained). An odd number of discarded ranks removes one more from the upper tail. Reject conversion or reduction overflow, including intermediate sum overflow. Do not change inputs. Selection, units, identities and interpretation belong to the caller; no model names, categories or fixed ensemble size are assumed.",
